language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Equal-sized groups: divide the sorted list a of N elements into k groups of consecutive elements by k-1 break points, so that all elements with the same value stay in one group, and the group sizes are as close as possible to round(N/k).
given a_dim1 : int
letting N = a_dim1
given a : matrix indexed by [int(1..N)] of int
given k : int
$ the target group size is N/k rounded to the nearest whole number (halves round up)
letting target = (2 * N + k) / (2 * k)
$ a break point may only come after the last element of a run of equal values, so these are the admissible break positions
letting boundary = [ i | i : int(1..N-1), a[i] != a[i + 1] ]
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..k-1)] of int(1..N-1)
$ ends[j] is the index of the last element of group j, with ends[0] = 0 for the start of the list
find ends : matrix indexed by [int(0..k)] of int(0..N)
find total_error : int(0..2 * N)

branching on [x]
minimising total_error
such that
$ the first group starts at the first element and the last group ends at the last element
ends[0] = 0,
ends[k] = N,
$ the break points are the ends of the groups, so each group is a run of consecutive elements
forAll j : int(1..k-1) . x[j] = ends[j],
$ each group has at least one element, so the ends increase
forAll j : int(1..k) . ends[j] > ends[j - 1],
$ a break point cannot split elements with the same value
forAll j : int(1..k-1) . x[j] in toSet(boundary),
$ the total error is the sum over the groups of the distance between each group size and the target size
total_error = (sum j : int(1..k) . |(ends[j] - ends[j - 1]) - target|)
